All working. Here's the final program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions(JsonSerializerDefaults.Web)
{
    TypeInfoResolver = new DefaultJsonTypeInfoResolver()
};

// 1. GetTypeInfo<T>() — strongly-typed metadata
JsonTypeInfo<Person> personInfo = options.GetTypeInfo<Person>();
string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Alice", 42), personInfo);

// 2. TryGetTypeInfo<T>() — check without throwing
var restrictedOptions = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    TypeInfoResolver = PersonOnlyContext.Default   // only knows Person
};

if (restrictedOptions.TryGetTypeInfo<UnknownType>(out _))
    Console.WriteLine("found");
else
    Console.WriteLine("not available — no exception thrown");
```

**Key APIs:**

| Method | Returns | Throws on missing? |
|--------|---------|---------------------|
| `GetTypeInfo<T>()` | `JsonTypeInfo<T>` | Yes |
| `TryGetTypeInfo<T>(out …)` | `bool` | No |

Both are .NET 11-only extension points on `JsonSerializerOptions` that give you a typed `JsonTypeInfo<T>` directly—no casting required.
